0 0 11.172 2H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414l8.704 8.704a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l6.58-6.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="7.5" cy="7.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg></div><h3 class="pg-card__title">Category-Specific Fees</h3><p class="pg-card__desc">Calculator adjusts fees by Walmart category (Electronics, Media, Hazmat, Oversize). No guessing.</p></div><div class="pg-card"><div class="pg-card__icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="pgx-55 lucide lucide-download" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 15V3"></path><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path><path d="m7 10 5 5 5-5"></path></svg></div><h3 class="pg-card__title">Export &amp; Track</h3><p class="pg-card__desc">Download results as CSV. Track fees over time. Monitor which categories are most expensive.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="pg-sec bg-shades"><div class="pg-wrap-3xl"><div><h2 class="pg-h2 pg-mb-4">When to Use WFS vs FBM vs 2-Step vs 3PL</h2><p class="pgx-96">WFS isn&#x27;t always the best choice. Use the calculator to compare options and decide which fulfillment method maximizes your profit.</p></div>
        <!-- <div class="pgx-182"><div class="pgx-94">Fulfillment comparison matrix</div></div> -->
        <div class="pgx-183"><p>WFS works best for standard-size items. Fees vary by weight, dimensions, and category. Use the calculator to estimate your specific costs and see whether WFS makes financial sense for your products.</p><p>WFS breaks down when items are heavy, oversized, or in restricted categories. A 5-lb item jumps to $4+ per unit. A hazmat or electronics item adds 50% surcharge. In those cases,<!-- --> <a class="pg-link" href="two-step-dropshipping.php">2-step dropshipping</a> <!-- -->or traditional 3PL might be cheaper.</p><p>FBM (Fulfillment By Merchant, i.e. you ship) is free for marketplace commission and can be profitable if you can ship fast and maintain high ratings. But FBM requires you to manage logistics, which costs time.</p><p>3PL (third-party logistics) is a middle ground: you pay ~$2-$5 per unit for full service, but get scale economies and dedicated customer service.</p><p>The calculator lets you input your specific products and see exact costs across methods. That data-driven decision-making is the difference between profitable sourcing and guessing.</p></div></div></section><section class="pgx-114 bg-shades"><div class="pg-wrap-4xl"><div class="pgx-46"><h3 class="pgx-115">Ready to Optimize Your Walmart Fulfillment?</h3><a class="gradient-bg shadow-btn pg-btn" href="pricing.php">Try Our Full Software Suite<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="pgx-3 lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div></section><section class="pg-sec pg-sec--alt"><div class="pg-wrap-3xl"><h2 class="pg-h2 pg-center pg-mb-12">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div><div class="pg-faq__item"><button class="pg-faq__btn"><span class="pg-faq__q">Does WFS include shipping?</span><span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="2